From: ArchPad project <archpad@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi846: calibrate MIPI timings and PLL for Xiaomi Pad 6

On Xiaomi Pad 6 (pipa), the front camera (AAC HI846W) is wired for 2 MIPI
CSI data lanes (Lanes 0 and 1, clock on Lane 7) on CSIPHY4.

This patch:
1. Configures 2-lane mode in hi846_init_2lane (0x0902 = 0x431a, 720 MHz VCO).
2. Adds 2-lane MIPI register sequence mode_3264x2448_mipi_2lane and
   mode_3264x1836_mipi_2lane with 0x0902 = 0x431a.
3. Populates reg_list_2lane for 3264x2448 and 3264x1836, and sets
   mipi_clk_div_2lane = 1 (720 MHz link frequency, 288 Mpix/s at 30 fps).
4. Configures 16-bit register writes for stream start (0x0a00 = 0x0100)
   and stream stop (0x0a00 = 0x0000).
5. Fixes frame_length calculation in hi846_set_video_mode() using pixel_rate.
6. Provides fallback in hi846_add_link_freqs() for Xiaomi Pad 6 link frequencies.
